.TH "PROFILER.SAMPLEBUFFERFULL_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Profiler.samplebufferfull_event \- Profiler: samplebufferfull event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]samplebufferfull\f[B]\f[R] event of the
\f[CR]Profiler\f[R] interface is fired when the number of samples the
profiler has recorded matches the \f[CR]maxBufferSize\f[R] value passed
to the profiler\(cqs constructor.
.PP
After this event fires, the profiler will not record any more samples.
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqsamplebufferfull\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onsamplebufferfull = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
An \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] profiler = \f[B]new\f[R] Profiler({ sampleInterval: 10, maxBufferSize: 100 });

profiler.addEventListener(\(dqsamplebufferfull\(dq, \f[B]async\f[R] () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(dqSample buffer full!\(dq);
  \f[B]const\f[R] trace = \f[B]await\f[R] profiler.stop();
  console.log(JSON.stringify(trace));
});
.EE
